"Textbook: OpenStax <em>Astronomy 2e</em>, §{#} (galaxy mergers) and §{#} (ocean tides and the Moon). Access for free at https://openstax.org/details/books/astronomy-2e.",
"<strong>Setups in the demo:</strong> two views. Collision: Tails: two equal disks; Spinning the other way; Bridge to a small companion; Tilted disks (the Mice); A dwarf torn into a stream; Andromeda is coming; Andromeda, faster sideways. Why stars miss: Stars almost never hit. This worksheet uses all but the Mice.",
"Each galaxy is a central mass carrying a disk of {#} test stars, gold for one galaxy and blue for the other. The two centers pull each other and every star; the stars do not pull each other. Closest approach sets how near the centers come.",
